  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "A father is currently eleven times his daughter’s age. In three years, the father’s age will be the square of his daughter’s age. Find the daughter’s present age.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "2 or 3 years.\n\nModel their ages in three years and factorise; both positive roots satisfy the conditions.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the daughter’s present age in years. The father’s present age is $11x$ years.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}11x+3&=(x+3)^2\\\\11x+3&=x^2+6x+9\\\\x^2-5x+6&=0\\\\(x-2)(x-3)&=0\\\\x&=2\\text{ or }3\\end{align*}$$\n\nIf $x=2$, their ages in three years are 5 and 25, and $25=5^2$. If $x=3$, their ages in three years are 6 and 36, and $36=6^2$. The daughter is presently 2 or 3 years old.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
